WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.839
The man was Roger Redbeard!

2
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:23.136
"W-what do you mean, you'll make us walk the plank?" Maggie asked nervously.

3
00:00:23.137 --> 00:00:28.260
Roger Redbeard grinned. "I'm just joking around, kids," he said.

4
00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:32.405
"I like to practice my pirate voice. Aargh!"

5
00:00:32.406 --> 00:00:34.919
Henry glanced at his friends.

6
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.100
He could tell they were thinking the same thing he was.

7
00:00:38.101 --> 00:00:40.582
Had Roger taken their tickets?

8
00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:46.250
"Excuse me, Mr. Redbeard," he said. "Can we ask you a question?"

9
00:00:46.251 --> 00:00:50.372
"Sure." Roger took a sip from the plastic cup he was holding.

10
00:00:50.373 --> 00:00:52.748
"Is it about pirates?"

11
00:00:52.749 --> 00:00:56.198
"Not exactly." Henry cleared his throat.

12
00:00:56.199 --> 00:01:01.151
"We're just wondering where you've been since the last time we saw you."

13
00:01:01.152 --> 00:01:05.632
Roger looked surprised. "I walked downtown to get lunch."

14
00:01:05.633 --> 00:01:08.915
Henry noticed that Roger was holding a plastic cup.

15
00:01:08.916 --> 00:01:15.129
It had a logo printed on it that said SCGS. "Why do you ask?"

16
00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:19.514
"No reason." Henry traded another look with his friends.

17
00:01:19.515 --> 00:01:23.510
"Um, did you see anyone else on the beach while you were walking?"

18
00:01:23.511 --> 00:01:27.790
Roger shrugged. "It's pretty quiet at this end of town.

19
00:01:27.791 --> 00:01:33.093
It's mostly private land. The only person I passed out here was the Jones girl."

20
00:01:33.094 --> 00:01:37.480
"The Jones girl?" Maggie said. "Who's that?"

21
00:01:37.481 --> 00:01:41.083
"Sorry, I don't remember her first name," Roger said.

22
00:01:41.084 --> 00:01:43.866
"But her parents own the general store in town."

23
00:01:43.867 --> 00:01:47.123
Henry realized Roger must be talking about Anna.

24
00:01:47.124 --> 00:01:50.086
"Did she see you?" he asked Roger.

25
00:01:50.087 --> 00:01:54.601
"I doubt it," Roger replied. "She was running through the surf."

26
00:01:54.602 --> 00:01:59.210
He took another sip of his drink. "Is that all you want to know?

27
00:01:59.211 --> 00:02:03.155
Because if you don't have any questions about pirates, I'd better move along."

28
00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:06.609
"Okay. Bye," Henry said.

29
00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:12.021
Roger wandered away, disappearing soon behind some rocks.

30
00:02:12.022 --> 00:02:14.502
Maggie checked to make sure he was gone.

31
00:02:14.503 --> 00:02:18.294
"Do you think he's telling the truth?" she asked.

32
00:02:18.295 --> 00:02:23.310
"He wasn't carrying that cup when we saw him before," Henry reminded her.

33
00:02:23.311 --> 00:02:26.291
"So he probably is telling the truth."

34
00:02:26.292 --> 00:02:30.135
"That means he couldn't have stolen our tickets," Cole said.

35
00:02:30.136 --> 00:02:35.411
"Not necessarily," Maggie argued. "How far away is the town?

36
00:02:35.412 --> 00:02:41.121
It might only take five minutes to walk there. We should ask William or Anna."

37
00:02:41.122 --> 00:02:45.816
"Speaking of Anna, shouldn't she be a suspect?" Henry asked.

38
00:02:45.817 --> 00:02:51.161
"Roger said he saw her running down the beach. That's kind of suspicious."

39
00:02:51.162 --> 00:02:53.443
"Not really," Maggie said.

40
00:02:53.444 --> 00:02:57.206
"She was looking for booty, just like the rest of us."

41
00:02:57.207 --> 00:03:02.555
Henry nodded. "But she was alone, while the rest of us had partners.

42
00:03:02.556 --> 00:03:06.712
And she knew exactly where all the tide pools were.

43
00:03:06.713 --> 00:03:12.236
What if she grabbed the tickets before Luke and Nathan reached the tide pool?" he asked.

44
00:03:12.237 --> 00:03:15.407
Maggie gasped. "You could be right!

45
00:03:15.408 --> 00:03:19.687
Nathan said he and Luke had trouble finding their tide pool."

46
00:03:19.688 --> 00:03:23.430
"But why would she want the tickets?" Cole wondered.

47
00:03:23.431 --> 00:03:26.131
"She's not even interested in pirates."

48
00:03:26.132 --> 00:03:32.200
"That's true." Henry thought back. "She said the legends were stupid."

49
00:03:32.201 --> 00:03:36.584
Just then they heard a shout. Luke was running toward them.

50
00:03:36.585 --> 00:03:41.027
"What is it?" Maggie called. "Did you find the booty?"

51
00:03:41.028 --> 00:03:44.157
"Maybe," Luke replied breathlessly.

52
00:03:44.158 --> 00:03:47.032
"We didn't find anything at the marina.

53
00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:51.054
I told the others I'd run and see if you guys found anything.

54
00:03:51.055 --> 00:03:58.727
But on the way here, I noticed something interesting. Come on!"

55
00:03:58.728 --> 00:04:05.858
He led the way back to the bay.

56
00:04:05.859 --> 00:04:09.111
A rowboat was bobbing in the water just offshore.

57
00:04:09.112 --> 00:04:12.787
A skull-and-crossbones flag was flying from it.

58
00:04:12.788 --> 00:04:16.217
"That's a pirate flag!" Cole exclaimed.

59
00:04:16.218 --> 00:04:21.154
"You guys pull in the boat. I'll run and get the others."

60
00:04:21.155 --> 00:04:25.513
The rowboat was tied to a small dock with strong rope.

61
00:04:25.514 --> 00:04:31.993
Henry, Maggie, and Luke pulled on the rope as Cole ran off.

62
00:04:31.994 --> 00:04:39.803
By the time Cole returned with Nathan, William, and Anna, the boat was on the beach.

63
00:04:39.804 --> 00:04:43.748
"There's a pirate chest on board!" Luke called.

64
00:04:43.749 --> 00:04:49.592
Cole helped Luke lift the chest out of the boat. Then Henry opened it.

65
00:04:49.593 --> 00:04:56.087
"Wow!" he cried when he saw what was inside. "Handheld video game players!

66
00:04:56.088 --> 00:05:00.223
There are seven of them, one for each of us!"

67
00:05:00.224 --> 00:05:06.336
"Are you kidding?" Maggie exclaimed. "Let me see!"

68
00:05:06.337 --> 00:05:09.006
She grabbed one of the players and turned it on.

69
00:05:09.007 --> 00:05:12.104
A picture of a pirate ship appeared on the screen.

70
00:05:12.105 --> 00:05:15.531
"Whoa!" Luke peered over Maggie's shoulder.

71
00:05:15.532 --> 00:05:19.752
"It's already loaded with the Revenge of the Pirate's Ghost game!"

72
00:05:19.753 --> 00:05:23.149
"No way!" Nathan yelled.

73
00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:25.706
"Can I have one?" Cole asked.

74
00:05:25.707 --> 00:05:32.433
The kids each grabbed one of the players. Anna was the last to take one.

75
00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:37.070
"I've been dying to get one of these," she said slowly.

76
00:05:37.071 --> 00:05:42.883
"My parents said they're too expensive, but I've been saving my allowance all summer."

77
00:05:42.884 --> 00:05:48.355
That made Henry stop and think. "You're right, Anna," Henry said.

78
00:05:48.356 --> 00:05:55.913
"These game players are expensive, a lot more expensive than a bunch of movie tickets, even for a premiere."

79
00:05:55.914 --> 00:06:02.386
"Yeah." Nathan sounded distracted as he played with his game. "So what?"

80
00:06:02.387 --> 00:06:10.604
Henry shrugged. "So why would someone steal the tickets, but not this booty?"
